=== PARITY (vs web FlagsTable.tsx) ===
  Shape: the web component is PRESENTATIONAL (props rows / loading / onEdit / onAskDelete). The native
  surface keeps that contract: rows + loading arrive through the P1/S8 seam (FlagsTableSource ->
  FlagsTableModel; the production app wires it over the shared admin-diagnostics state holder), and the
  row actions stay parent-owned via the view's onEdit / onAskDelete callbacks. The view performs NO HTTP.

  Data sources -> bound via the seam + UI hooks:
    useTranslation -> the P1/S10 FlagsTableStrings facade (every Text routes through it).
    useSortToggle  -> ported as FlagsSortToggle (field=key, asc default, toggle flips direction) + the
                      pure FlagsSort.sorted port of `a.key.localeCompare(b.key) * dir`. Rows are fed to
                      the shared TSDataTable in the web default order (key asc); the key column also
                      carries a comparator so the shared table's HIG-native sort lets users re-sort.

  Value preview -> FlagsValuePreview.preview is a 1:1 port of the web `previewValue`: null->"null",
    undefined->"\u2014", string->JSON.stringify (quoted+escaped), boolean/number->String(value),
    array/object->compact JSON (sorted keys) truncated to 117 chars + "\u2026" past 120. EXECUTED below
    (28/28).

  Composition -> glass panel (web card) · header (freshness chip + refresh) · TSDataTable (web
    `DataTable`) with the three web columns: key (monospaced, text-primary), value (monospaced, muted,
    single-line middle-truncated), actions (Edit = secondary + pencil -> onEdit; Delete = destructive +
    trash -> onAskDelete). Recharts->none / Leaflet->none. Native pagination = lazy scrolling (HIG) in
    place of the web 25/50/100 pager; the iPhone compact width renders the shared table's card layout
    (web `mobileColumns`).

  States (all render) -> loading (skeleton rows + "Loading flags\u2026" a11y) · empty ("No feature flags
    are set on this server.") · error (Retry, web QueryError equivalent) · stale (chip + banner) ·
    offline (cached rows + chip + banner) · content. FlagsTableModel.resolvePhase keeps cached rows
    visible behind refresh / errors; loading-with-no-rows -> loading and loaded/empty-with-no-rows ->
    empty reproduce the web `emptyMessage = loading ? 'Loading flags\u2026' : 'No feature flags\u2026'`.

  i18n -> all 7 web source keys (admin.flags.cols.{key,value,actions}, admin.flags.actions.{edit,delete},
    admin.flags.table.{loading,empty}) + the native chrome/a11y keys resolve through the P1/S10 facade
    with the web t(key,default) fallback. Used-vs-defined diff = 0 (20 used = 20 defined; see [i18n]
    below). No English literals in native code (only the sanctioned facade fallbacks).

  a11y -> container carries a localized summary (count of flags / empty message); each row exposes a
    "key, value" label; Edit/Delete buttons + refresh carry accessibilityLabel (the actions scoped to
    the flag key); Dynamic Type via Font.TS tokens; no custom animations (system / reduce-motion safe).

  Telemetry -> FlagsTableModel.start() emits viewOpened(surface:"FlagsTable") (P1/S11 view.opened);
    OSLogFlagsTableTelemetry is the default, the production app injects the shared Telemetry adapter.
    Asserted by a spy test (typecheck-covered in [1]).

